<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      Deliberately does NOT override `window_background` / `splash_background`.

      Those two are the *launch* colours, painted by the system before Compose draws anything. The
      app's theme default is Light on a fresh install regardless of the Android system theme (see
      `AppSettings.theme`, `SettingsRepository`'s fallback and `JustTheCarbsTheme`'s default), so a
      dark launch window on a dark-system phone produced a visible near-black → cream flash that
      contradicted the app's own default.

      The launch window cannot read DataStore — the preference is not available until after the
      first frame — so it cannot follow the user's actual choice. Between a flash for every
      dark-system user on every launch and a stable branded light splash for everyone, the stable
      one wins: it is correct for the default, and for a user who has explicitly chosen Dark it is a
      brief branded plate rather than a wrong-colour flash of the app's own UI.

      An explicitly-selected Dark theme still applies in full as soon as Compose composes; only this
      pre-first-frame window is unconditionally light.
    -->
</resources>
